# Activity — the engineer's window, not a brain

- **No Postgres from Python.** Cases/events/artifacts go through the n8n webhook `MAS — Control Plane Proxy` (`app/control_plane.py`, operations `schema`, `snapshot`, `list_cases`, `upsert_agent`, …). `CONTROL_PLANE_PROXY_URL` empty = memory mode = lab only.
- Live API (`app/cases_api.py`): `GET/POST /cases`, `GET /cases/{id}`, `/state`, `/events`, `/errors`, `POST /cases/{id}/events` (agents write progress here, **no** Excel `X-API-Key`), `POST /cases/{id}/answer` (HITL), `POST /cases/{id}/run` (create/resume/restart → orchestrator webhook `mas-orchestrator-step`), `GET /cases/{id}/artifacts/{artifact_id}`, `GET /cases/{id}/stream`. `/v1/tasks*` is the older Entry-Form contour — do not extend.
- Activity does not decide anything about the domain. It stores the raw engineer answer (`choice`, `text`, `label`, files) and resumes the orchestrator (`action=resume`, `source=human`); interpretation happens in the orchestrator. Do not parse free-text answers here.
- Artifacts (`app/state_shape.py`): flat ids `excel`, `excel_1…`, `schedule_source`, `schedule_source_N` (includes), `schedule_out`, `diff`, `surface`, `trajectory_N`; `nest_artifacts`/`flatten_artifacts` must be lossless — the first workbook owns `excel`, the rest are `attachments[role=excel]`. The JS twin lives in `n8n/templates/mas_state_utils.py`; change both, test both.
- `_artifact_slot` / `_promote_schedule_root`: the multipart `file` is Excel or SCHEDULE by extension; `schedule_files` are baseline + includes; `attachments` are extra workbooks/trajectories. Keep filenames — agents show them to engineers via `data`, never in `message`.
- UI (`static/app.js`, `index.html`): renders `status_message`, HITL questions with `options[{value,label}]` as buttons + free text + file upload; `case.finished` shows the orchestrator's `summary_for_human`. Bump the cache-bust `?v=` when changing static files. Never render technical ids to the engineer.
- **Developer log is the only place for technical detail** (`app/case_log.py`, `GET /cases/{id}/log`, `static/log.js` behind the «Режим разработчика» toggle). Event kinds prefixed `trace.` never reach the chat (`is_trace_kind`); new technical detail goes into event `payload` and shows up in the log's `detail`, not in `status_message`. `level`/`source`/`title` are derived deterministically in `case_log.py` — extend those functions for a new kind, do not special-case in JS. Execution links need `execution_id` + `workflow_id` in the payload and `N8N_PUBLIC_URL` (browser-facing n8n).
- Field: Windows `.venv`, `setup-windows.bat` / `start-windows.bat`, listens on `0.0.0.0:8200`; started **after** the proxy is Active. Lab: `docker compose restart mas-activity` (bind-mounted code).

## Verify
```bash
cd mas-activity-service && PYTHONPATH=. .venv/bin/python -m pytest -q tests
python3 scripts/mas_trace_case.py --last        # timeline/state/text audit of the newest case
```
